sequenceDiagram
  %% Target design: docs/reference/feature-flow.md section 6, one Swamp workflow per Gateway release, manual or automatic.
  %% A failed check switches back; migrations are expand and contract. docs/reference/gateway-recovery.md#release-as-a-swamp-run.
  %% status: draft
  %% command: gateway:release:deploy
  %% kind: gateway.release
  %% behavior name: gateway-release-<step>-209 (fixed)
  autonumber
  %% lane TR icon=terminal pill=caller tone=gray
  %% lane GW icon=gateway pill=intent tone=blue
  %% lane SW icon=workflow pill=executes tone=green
  %% lane AC icon=workflow pill=child tone=green
  %% lane GN icon=server pill=target tone=amber
  participant TR as CLI<br/>orbit · MCP
  participant GW as Gateway<br/>Laravel API
  participant SW as Swamp<br/>serve on Node 209
  participant AC as Activate run<br/>child · new commit
  participant GN as Gateway Node<br/>Node 14
  TR->>GW: gateway:release:deploy<br/>full sha
  %%> Command:
  %%> - `orbit gateway:release:deploy <full sha>`; the automatic tick admits the newest green commit the same way
  Note over GW: Admit the release<br/>verify agent pin · web build
  %%> Requirements:
  %%> - the full commit; no other release queued or running
  %%> - the agent pin passes its Sigstore check; CI published the commit's web build
  %%> Result:
  %%> - a running release record; the pin, artifact, Horizon unit and SSH targets frozen as inputs
  GW->>SW: Start run, full intent<br/>operation-gateway-release
  %%> What it does:
  %%> - at run start, mints one read token (contents, actions) into the vault
  GW-->>TR: 202 Accepted<br/>running release record
  SW->>GN: Fetch the commit<br/>shared repository
  %%> What it does:
  %%> - fetches the commit with the read token when the shared repository lacks it; the token reaches git only in its environment
  %%> Decided by the orchestrator, for Nick's review:
  %%> - the fetch is its own step, so that the build runs its script from the commit being released, not from the live release
  SW->>GN: Build the release<br/>worktree · composer · REVISION
  %%> What it does:
  %%> - refuses a commit that does not descend from the current release
  %%> - links shared env and storage, installs dependencies, seals with `REVISION` and a cached config
  %%> - a sealed release of the commit is reused
  SW->>GN: Install the web build<br/>artifact · digest · rename
  SW->>GN: Snapshot the database<br/>VACUUM INTO
  SW->>GN: Migrate<br/>artisan migrate --isolated
  %%> What it does:
  %%> - prints the end of the migration's output and its exit code; a failed exec would keep no output
  Note over SW: Check the migration<br/>assert the exit code
  %%> On failure:
  %%> - from here until the switch, the release pauses with the old release live
  %%> - the record's message ends with the migration's output
  Note over SW: Load Swamp on Node 209<br/>operation-gateway-swamp-load
  %%> What it does:
  %%> - the load child: checkout, grants the new release rendered, serve reload
  SW->>GN: Admit VM refreshes<br/>artisan · new release
  %%> What it does:
  %%> - runs `task-vms:refresh-images --commit <sha>` from the new release: one `task_vm.image_refresh` run per task VM host, admitted by the new commit's code, started on the workflows the load installed, and running while the release goes on to switch (docs/cli/tasks/vm-image-refresh.mmd)
  %%> - every release refreshes, code-only ones too: the base holds the warm checkout and the nested Gateway agent of the commit
  %%> - Swamp has only just reloaded, so a host whose run Swamp cannot take yet (`swamp.vault_sync_unavailable`) is asked again, up to 6 rounds 5 s apart; the other hosts are not held
  %%> On failure:
  %%> - best effort: the release never fails for it, and the hand-over waits only for the admission, a few seconds
  %%> - it runs before the switch, so a release that later fails or switches back has refreshed the base to its commit; the next release refreshes again
  Note over SW: Hand over the release<br/>gateway-release-activate
  %%> Why:
  %%> - the child runs from the definition the load installed, so the switch runs the new commit's steps
  AC->>GN: Drain Horizon<br/>systemctl stop · SIGTERM only
  %%> What it does:
  %%> - waits until the unit's whole control group is empty, as long as the drain allows; Horizon's jobs open SSH connections of their own, so no shared connection master stays in the group, and the wait covers any other process a job leaves
  %%> - refuses to stop a unit that lacks the stop policy (`KillMode=mixed`, `SendSIGKILL=no`), because it would kill a running job
  %%> On failure:
  %%> - the run fails with `gateway.release_horizon_unit_stale` for a unit without the policy, or `gateway.release_horizon_not_drained` when the unit did not stop in time; Horizon is started again below
  AC->>GN: Switch the release<br/>gateway-rollback · Horizon
  %%> Why:
  %%> - the same script an operator rolls back with: links, PHP-FPM reload, running services restart
  AC->>GN: Verify the Gateway<br/>/up · status version
  opt the check failed
    AC->>GN: Switch back<br/>gateway-rollback previous
  end
  AC->>GN: Start Horizon<br/>always · also after a failure
  %%> Why:
  %%> - the release drained Horizon, so every end of the run leaves it running: the old release after a failed drain or a switch back, the new one after a verified switch
  %%> - starting a running unit changes nothing
  %%> Decided by the orchestrator, for Nick's review:
  %%> - the drain relies on the unit's stop policy alone; the rollback script no longer starts a stopped Horizon, because this step does after every end of the run
  AC->>GN: Resume document cleanup<br/>best effort
  %%> Why:
  %%> - the scheduler restart paused the release cleanups; one that stays paused never fails the release
  AC->>GN: Prune old releases<br/>best effort
  alt every step succeeded
    SW-->>GW: Run succeeded<br/>terminal result
    Note over GW: Record verified<br/>fleet rollout follows
    %%> Next:
    %%> - the Gateway queues one `fleet.rollout` admission for the Nodes behind this commit (`fleet:rollout`)
  else a step before Migrate fails
    SW--xGW: Run failed<br/>failed step
    Note over GW: Mark failed<br/>nothing changed · rerun safe
  else the check failed, switched back
    SW--xGW: Run failed<br/>failed step
    Note over GW: Record switched back<br/>alert · next commit releases
  else another step from Migrate on fails
    SW--xGW: Run failed<br/>failed step
    Note over GW: Pause automatic releases<br/>snapshot named · alert
  end
